e array `parent` represents a valid tree rooted at node 0.","problemLink":"https://leetcode.com/problems/weighted-sum-of-a-tree/","problemName":"Weighted Sum of a Tree","problemNumber":4015,"problemSlug":"weighted-sum-of-a-tree","schemaVersion":2,"sequenceIndex":4015,"solutionApproaches":[]},{"assets":[{"assetIndex":0,"bytes":26252,"contentType":"image/png","localPath":"leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4016-maximum-area-of-two-non-overlapping-square-submatrices/4016-image.png","originalUrl":"../../../images/4016-image.png","sha256":"3b92e245e127ab72e302d14ffb596e11cf0e8f84b25b7fe5951f4ee2340552ba"},{"assetIndex":1,"bytes":10778,"contentType":"image/png","localPath":"leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4016-maximum-area-of-two-non-overlapping-square-submatrices/4016-screenshot-2026-06-13-at-83728pm.png","originalUrl":"../../../images/4016-screenshot-2026-06-13-at-83728pm.png","sha256":"5c830faef2f91c55e383708c4c5dc8b3cec5d49174e5a8d06e48109c6c15744f"},{"assetIndex":2,"bytes":5563,"contentType":"image/png","localPath":"leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4016-maximum-area-of-two-non-overlapping-square-submatrices/4016-screenshot-2026-06-13-at-83751pm.png","originalUrl":"../../../images/4016-screenshot-2026-06-13-at-83751pm.png","sha256":"965c144cf09f455dd0c1675364cb1b9f9648a60a28cd5d6b7df08750c452467d"}],"categories":["Array","Dynamic Programming","Matrix"],"constraintBlocks":[],"contentBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"You are given a 2D integer matrix `mat` of size `m × n`, where:\n\n- `mat[r][c] == 1` means the cell at row `r` and column `c` is usable.\n\n- `mat[r][c] == 0` means it is not usable.\n\nYour task is to find **two [submatrices](leetcode-keyword)** that satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- Both submatrices must be squares of the same side length `k`.\n\n- The two submatrices must not share any cell.\n\n- Each submatrix can only cover cells where `mat[r][c] == 1`.\n\nReturn the **maximum possible area** of each of the two squares. If it is not possible to choose two suc